The production implementation is pure Go. The current source tree and
production builds contain and distribute no Qoder CLI qoder_auth WebAssembly
module. The root Go module and production builds do not depend on wazero.
The optional standalone analysis tool under tools/wasm_oracle is a separate
Go module with its own dependencies, including wazero.

This statement about the current source tree and production builds does not
apply to every historical revision: commit 09452a6 contained a vendor WASM
asset, which was removed in commit baa9052. The Git history retains those
revisions; removal from the current tree does not remove historical copies
or grant redistribution rights to that asset.

The optional analysis tools under tools/ can validate and execute an
authorized, operator-supplied, version-pinned Qoder CLI 1.1.34 or 1.1.74
WebAssembly module as an external interoperability oracle. That external
module is not included in the current source tree or covered by this
project's AGPL-3.0 license. Operators are responsible for confirming their
right to possess and execute it and must not redistribute it without the
applicable permissions.

The current source tree does not distribute official Qoder CLI binaries,
real user credentials, captured live traffic, private model catalogs, or
local account data. Test fixtures contain synthetic data only. Users must
use their own authorized account and subscription and comply with applicable
service terms and law.
